; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be sent if Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and not request/DER-Flags bit ERP-Re-Authentication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-context-identifier)
; AVP: Context-Identifier
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP was not set in the initial Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-apn-oi-replacement)
; AVP: APN-OI-Replacement
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP was not set in the initial Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-apn-configuration)
; AVP: APN-Configuration
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if the non-3GPP access network was decided to be trusted, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP was not set in the initial Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-ambr)
; AVP: AMBR
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present only if the non-3GPP access network was decided to be trusted, the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS and ANID is \"HRPD\"."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-mip-fa-rk)
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be present if MIPv4 is used, MN-FA authentication extension is supported and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-mip-fa-rk-spi)
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK-SPI
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be present if MIP-FA-RK is present"
    present-if MIP-FA-RK


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-trace-info)
; AVP: Trace-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be included if the subscriber and equipment trace has been activated for the user in the HSS and signalling based activation is used to download the trace activation from the HSS to the trusted non-3GPP access network."
    text-only
"Only the Trace-Data AVP shall be included to the Trace-Info AVP"
    members only Trace-Data


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-subscription-id)
; AVP: Subscription-Id
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall contain the MSISDN of the UE and shall be sent if it is available and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Subscription-Id/Subscription-Id-Type = END_USER_E164


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-wlcp-key)
; AVP: WLCP-Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS and the TWAN Connection Mode previously selected is MCM."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-emergency-info)
; AVP: Emergency-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present for a non-roaming authenticated user, if this information was received from the HSS, the TWAN indicated support of IMS Emergency Sessions and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-ue-usage-type)
; AVP: UE-Usage-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if this information is available in the user subscription."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-reauth-dea-mps-priority)
; AVP: MPS-Priority
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Based on operator policy, this information element shall be sent to the non-3GPP access network if the UE has an MPS subscription in the HSS."
    text-only


; Type: Information Elements
; Command: Session-Termination-Request ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-command-5-1-2-4-1-1)
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.4.1 ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-command-section-5-1-2-4-1-1)
; Section: 5.1.2.4.1
; Table: 5.1.2.4.1/1
; Page: 63
; Columns: Name             AVP                 Cat
"Permanent User Identity"   User-Name           M
"Termination Cause"         Termination-Cause   M


; Type: Information Elements
; Command: Session-Termination-Answer ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-command-5-1-2-4-1-2)
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.4.2 ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-command-section-5-1-2-4-1-2)
; Section: 5.1.2.4.1
; Table: 5.1.2.4.1/2
; Page: 63
; Columns: Name   AVP                               Cat
Result            Result-Code/Experimental-Result   M


; Type: Information Elements
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-command-5-1-2-5-1-1)
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1 ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-command-section-5-1-2-5-1-1)
; Section: 5.1.2.5.1
; Table: 5.1.2.5.1/1
; Page: 64
; Columns: Name                 AVP                 Cat
KeyName-NAI                     User-Name           M
EAP-Initiate                    EAP-Payload         M ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-eap-payload-5-1-2-5-1-1)
"Authentication Request Type"   Auth-Request-Type   M
DER-Flags                       DER-Flags           M


; Type: Information Elements
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-command-5-1-2-5-1-2)
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2 ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-command-section-5-1-2-5-1-2)
; Section: 5.1.2.5.1
; Table: 5.1.2.5.1/2
; Page: 64
; Columns: Name                 AVP                                        Cat
KeyName-NAI                     User-Name                                  M
EAP-Finish                      "EAP payload"                              O
"Authentication Request Type"   Auth-Request-Type                          M
"Result code"                   "Result-Code / Experimental Result Code"   M
"ERP Keying Material"           Key                                        C


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-erp-dea-key)
; AVP: Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Request-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.5.1
; Table: 5.1.2.5.1/2
; Page: 64
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if the ERP re-authentication is successful."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and request/DER-Flags bit ERP-Re-Authentication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#service-selection-labels)
; AVP: Service-Selection
; Section: 5.2.3.5
; Page: 74
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The contents of the Service-Selection AVP shall be formatted as a character string composed of one or more labels separated by dots (\".\")."
    encoding labels


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#anid-element)
; AVP: ANID
; Section: 5.2.3.7
; Page: 75
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The ANID AVP is of type UTF8String; this AVP contains the Access Network Identity; see"
    encoding element TS24.302 8.1.1 "Access Network Identity"


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: AN-Trusted
; Section: 5.2.3.9
; Page: 75
AN-Trusted ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 1503 10415 >
        TRUSTED   = 0
        UNTRUSTED = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-feature-list-id)
; AVP: Feature-List-ID
; Within: Supported-Features
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.2.3.10
; Page: 75
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"For this release, the Feature-List-ID AVP value shall be set to 1 for the STa/SWa application."
    values 1 if Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#mip-fa-rk-element)
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK
; Section: 5.2.3.12
; Page: 75
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The MIP-FA-RK AVP is of type OctetString; this AVP contains the FA-RK used to calculate the security parameters needed for the MN-FA authentication extension as defined by"
    encoding element TS33.402 9.2.1.2.2 "FA-RK"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#mip-fa-rk-spi-element)
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK-SPI
; Section: 5.2.3.13
; Page: 75
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The MIP-FA-RK-SPI AVP is of type Unsigned32; this AVP contains the security index used in identifying the security context for the FA-RK as defined by"
    encoding element TS33.402 9.2.1.2.2 "FA-RK-SPI"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#full-network-name-element)
; AVP: Full-Network-Name
; Section: 5.2.3.14
; Page: 75
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The Full-Network-Name AVP is of type OctetString; this AVP shall contain the Full Network Name and be encoded as the Full name value field of the AT_FULL_NAME_FOR_NETWORK attribute specified in clause 8.2.5.1"
    encoding element TS24.302 8.2.5.1 "Full name value"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#short-network-name-element)
; AVP: Short-Network-Name
; Section: 5.2.3.15
; Page: 75
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The Short-Network-Name AVP is of type OctetString; this AVP shall contain the Short Network Name and be encoded as the Short name value field of the AT_SHORT_NAME_FOR_NETWORK attribute specified in clause 8.2.5.2"
    encoding element TS24.302 8.2.5.2 "Short name value"


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: WLAN-Identifier
; Section: 5.2.3.18
; Page: 76
WLAN-Identifier ::= < AVP header: 1509 10415 >
        [ SSID ]
        [ HESSID ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Transport-Access-Type
; Section: 5.2.3.19
; Page: 76
Transport-Access-Type ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 1519 10415 >
        BBF = 0


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: DER-Flags
; Kind: bits
; Section: 5.2.3.20
; Table: 5.2.3.20/1
; Page: 76
NSWO-Capability-Indication      = 0
TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator = 1
IMEI-Check-Required-In-VPLMN    = 2
IMEI-Check-Request-In-VPLMN     = 3
Emergency-Capability-Indication = 4
ERP-Support-Indication          = 5
ERP-Re-Authentication           = 6


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#der-flags-undefined-bits)
; AVP: DER-Flags
; Section: 5.2.3.20
; Table: 5.2.3.20/1
; Page: 76
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sender and discarded by the receiver of the command."
    bits only 0 1 2 3 4 5 6


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: DEA-Flags
; Kind: bits
; Section: 5.2.3.21
; Table: 5.2.3.21/1
; Page: 77
NSWO-Authorization              = 0
TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator = 1
IMEI-Check-Request-In-VPLMN     = 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#dea-flags-undefined-bits)
; AVP: DEA-Flags
; Section: 5.2.3.21
; Table: 5.2.3.21/1
; Page: 77
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sender and discarded by the recever of the command."
    bits only 0 1 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#ssid-length)
; AVP: SSID
; Section: 5.2.3.22
; Page: 78
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall contain a string of 1 to 32 octets."
    length 1..32 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#hessid-mac-address)
; AVP: HESSID
; Section: 5.2.3.23
; Page: 78
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The HESSID AVP is of type UTF8String and it shall contain a 6-octet MAC address that identifies the Homogenous Extended Service Set (see IEEE Std 802.11-2012 [40]). It shall be encoded in upper-case ASCII characters with the octet values separated by dash characters. It shall contain a string of 17 octets."
    encoding mac-address
    length 17 octets


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Access-Network-Info
; Section: 5.2.3.24
; Page: 78
Access-Network-Info ::= < AVP header: 1526 10415 >
        [ SSID ]
        [ BSSID ]
        [ Location-Information ]
        [ Location-Data ]
        [ Operator-Name ]
        [ Logical-Access-ID ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#access-network-info-ssid)
; AVP: Access-Network-Info
; Section: 5.2.3.24
; Page: 78
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"For a Trusted WLAN, it shall contain the SSID of the WLAN and, unless otherwise determined by the TWAN operator's policies, it shall contain at least one of the following elements:"
"For an untrusted WLAN, it shall contain the same information as specified above for a trusted WLAN, where the operator name indicates the WLAN operator name."
    members at-least-one SSID


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#access-network-info-location-information)
; AVP: Location-Information
; Within: Access-Network-Info
; Section: 5.2.3.24
; Page: 78
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"the content of Location-Information shall indicate that the encoding follows a civic location profile, by setting the \"Code\" field to 0."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#access-network-info-operator-name)
; AVP: Operator-Name
; Within: Access-Network-Info
; Section: 5.2.3.24
; Page: 78
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Only values \"1\" (Realm) and \"2\" (E212, containing MCC and MNC values) shall be used in this specification."
    text-only


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: TWAN-Connection-Mode
; Kind: bits
; Section: 5.2.3.25
; Table: 5.2.3.25/1
; Page: 79
TSC-MODE = 0
SC-MODE  = 1
MC-MODE  = 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#twan-connection-mode-undefined-bits)
; AVP: TWAN-Connection-Mode
; Section: 5.2.3.25
; Table: 5.2.3.25/1
; Page: 79
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sender and discarded by the receiver of the command."
    bits only 0 1 2


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.2.3.26
; Page: 79
TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters ::= < AVP header: 1528 10415 >
        [ Connectivity-Flags ]
        [ Service-Selection ]
        [ PDN-Type ]
     *2 [ Served-Party-IP-Address ]
        [ TWAN-PCO ]
        [ TWAG-UP-Address ]
        [ TWAN-S2a-Failure-Cause ]
        [ SM-Back-Off-Timer ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#twan-connectivity-parameters-service-selection)
; AVP: Service-Selection
; Within: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.2.3.26
; Page: 79
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall contain both the network identifier part and the operator identifier part of the Access Point Name."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#twan-connectivity-parameters-pdn-type)
; AVP: PDN-Type
; Within: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.2.3.26
; Page: 79
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It may be set to IPv4, IPv6 or IPv4v6."
    range 0..2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#twan-connectivity-parameters-served-party-ip-address)
; AVP: Served-Party-IP-Address
; Within: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.2.3.26
; Page: 79
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"These AVPs shall be present if the S2a connection was successfully established, and they shall contain either of:"
    encoding ip-address
"For the IPv6 interface identifier, the higher 64 bits of the address shall be set to zero."
    text-only


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: Connectivity-Flags
; Kind: bits
; Section: 5.2.3.27
; Table: 5.2.3.26/1
; Page: 80
Initial-Attach-Indicator = 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#connectivity-flags-undefined-bits)
; AVP: Connectivity-Flags
; Section: 5.2.3.27
; Table: 5.2.3.26/1
; Page: 80
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sender and discarded by the receiver of the command."
    bits only 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#twag-cp-address-ip)
; AVP: TWAG-CP-Address
; Section: 5.2.3.29
; Page: 80
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The TWAG-CP-Address AVP is of type Address and shall contain the TWAG control-plane IPv4 and/or IPv6 address that the TWAG supports, to be used for WLCP by the UE if MCM is selected."
    encoding ip-address


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#twag-up-address-mac-address)
; AVP: TWAG-UP-Address
; Section: 5.2.3.30
; Page: 80
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The TWAG-UP-Address AVP is of type UTF8String and shall contain a 6-octet MAC address that identifies the TWAG user-plane MAC address to be used for encapsulating user plane packets between the UE and the TWAN, when SCM is used."
"It shall be encoded in upper-case ASCII characters with the octet values separated by dash characters. It shall contain a string of 17 octets."
    encoding mac-address
    length 17 octets


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: TWAN-S2a-Failure-Cause
; Kind: values
; Section: 5.2.3.31
; Table: 5.2.3.30/1
; Page: 80
"Insufficient resources"                            = 26
"Unknown APN"                                       = 27
"User authentication failed"                        = 29
"Request rejected by TWAN or PDN GW"                = 30
"Request rejected, unspecified"                     = 31
"Service option not supported"                      = 32
"Requested service option not subscribed"           = 33
"Service option temporarily out of order"           = 34
"Network failure"                                   = 38
"PDN type IPv4 only allowed"                        = 50
"PDN type IPv6 only allowed"                        = 51
"PDN connection does not exist"                     = 54
"Multiple accesses to a PDN connection not allowed" = 113


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#wlcp-key-element)
; AVP: WLCP-Key
; Section: 5.2.3.33
; Page: 81
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The WLCP-Key AVP (AVP Code 1535) is of type OctetString and it shall contain the WLCP Key used for protecting the WLCP signalling between the UE and the TWAN, as specified in"
    encoding element TS33.402 A.3 "WLCP key"


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: IMEI-Check-In-VPLMN-Result
; Kind: values
; Section: 5.2.3.35
; Table: 5.2.3.35/1
; Page: 81
Successful = 0
Illegal_ME = 1


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: High-Priority-Access-Info
; Kind: bits
; Section: 5.2.3.36
; Table: 5.2.3.36/1
; Page: 82
HPA_Configured = 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#high-priority-access-info-undefined-bits)
; AVP: High-Priority-Access-Info
; Section: 5.2.3.36
; Table: 5.2.3.36/1
; Page: 82
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sending TWAN and discarded by the receiving AAA Server."
    bits only 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-der-5-2-2-1-1-no-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.2.4
; Page: 82
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"In order to indicate that the session state is to be maintained, the Diameter client and server shall not include the Auth-Session-State AVP, either in the request or in the response messages"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-dea-5-2-2-1-2-no-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.2.4
; Page: 82
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"In order to indicate that the session state is to be maintained, the Diameter client and server shall not include the Auth-Session-State AVP, either in the request or in the response messages"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#sta-asa-5-2-2-2-2-no-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Abort-Session-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.2.2
; Section: 5.2.4
