; Table: 6.1.2.1.1-1
; Page: 83
; Columns: Name                                   AVP                            Cat
"User Identity"                                   User-Name                      M
"EAP payload"                                     EAP-Payload                    M ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-eap-payload-6-1-2-1-1-1)
"Authentication Request Type"                     Auth-Request-Type              M
"UE Layer-2 address"                              Calling-Station-Id             M ;; corrected: (TS29.273.py#elements-calling-station-id-6-1-2-1-1-1)
"Supported 3GPP QoS profile"                      QoS-Capability                 O
"Mobility Capabilities"                           MIP6-Feature-Vector            C
"Access Type"                                     RAT-Type                       M
"Access Network Identity"                         ANID                           M
"Visited Network Identifier"                      Visited-Network-Identifier     M
"Full Name for Network"                           Full-Network-Name              O
"Short Name for Network"                          Short-Network-Name             O
"APN Id"                                          Service-Selection              O
"Terminal Information"                            Terminal-Information           O
"Trust Relationship Indicator"                    AN-Trusted                     O
"Selected Trusted WLAN Identifier"                WLAN-Identifier                O
"DER Flags"                                       DER-Flags                      O
"Transport Access Type"                           Transport-Access-Type          C
"Supported TWAN Connection Modes"                 TWAN-Connection-Mode           O
"Provided Connectivity Parameters"                TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters   C
"TWAG Control Plane IP Address"                   TWAG-CP-Address                C
"Domain-Specific Re-authentication Key Request"   ERP-RK-Request                 O
"High Priority Access Info"                       High-Priority-Access-Info      C


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#swd-der-mip6-feature-vector)
; AVP: MIP6-Feature-Vector
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.1
; Section: 6.1.2.1.1
; Table: 6.1.2.1.1-1
; Page: 83
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The PMIP6_SUPPORTED flag and/or the GTPv2_SUPPORTED flag shall be set if the trusted non-3GPP access network supports PMIPv6 and/or GTPv2."
"The flag MIP6_INTEGRATED shall be set if DHCPv6 based Home Agent address discovery is supported as defined in IETF RFC 5447 [6]."
"The MIP4_SUPPORTED flag shall be set if the trusted non-3GPP access supports MIPv4 FA-CoA mode."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#swd-der-transport-access-type)
; AVP: Transport-Access-Type
; Section: 6.1.2.1.1
; Table: 6.1.2.1.1-1
; Page: 83
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"if the access network needs to receive the IMSI of the UE in the authentication response, then this information element shall be present, and it shall contain the value \"BBF\" (see clause 5.2.3.19)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#swd-der-twan-connectivity-parameters)
; AVP: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.1
; Section: 6.1.2.1.1
; Table: 6.1.2.1.1-1
; Page: 83
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be present if the 3GPP AAA Server has previously authorized the SCM to be used for EPC access."
"If the requested connectivity has been granted, the following information elements shall be included:"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#swd-der-full-network-name)
; AVP: Full-Network-Name
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.1
; Section: 6.1.2.1.1
; Table: 6.1.2.1.1-1
; Page: 83
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"If the Visited Network Identifier is present, this AVP shall be set."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#swd-der-short-network-name)
; AVP: Short-Network-Name
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.1
; Section: 6.1.2.1.1
; Table: 6.1.2.1.1-1
; Page: 83
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"If the Visited Network Identifier is present, this AVP shall be set."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#swd-der-twag-cp-address)
; AVP: TWAG-CP-Address
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.1
; Section: 6.1.2.1.1
; Table: 6.1.2.1.1-1
; Page: 83
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The TWAN shall include this IE if it indicates support of the MCM in the Supported TWAN Connection Modes IE."
    present-if TWAN-Connection-Mode bit MC-MODE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.273.dadx#swd-der-high-priority-access-info)
; AVP: High-Priority-Access-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.1
; Section: 6.1.2.1.1
; Table: 6.1.2.1.1-1
; Page: 83
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be sent to the 3GPP AAA Server if the UE has access priority"
    text-only


